    "result_text": "The build is green: **BUILD SUCCESS**, 21 tests run, 0 failures/errors/skipped.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented address normalization in `OwnerRestControllerV1.java`, applied whenever an owner is created via `POST /api/owners`.\n\n**New `normalizeAddress` method** performs, in order:\n1. Trim and collapse internal whitespace runs to a single space\n2. Upper-case\n3. Expand common street-type abbreviations on a per-word basis: `ST\u2192STREET`, `RD\u2192ROAD`, `AVE\u2192AVENUE`\n\nA `null` or whitespace-only address normalizes to the empty string, and the transformation is idempotent.\n\n**Wiring changes in `addOwner`:**\n- The address is normalized once up front; the normalized value is set on the owner so it is **stored and returned** (e.g. `\"  12  main  st \"` \u2192 `\"12 MAIN STREET\"`, `\"7 elm ave\"` \u2192 `\"7 ELM AVENUE\"`).\n- `rejectMissingOrBlankFields` now checks the **normalized** address, so an address blank after normalization (e.g. `\"   \"`) is rejected with 400.\n- `rejectDuplicateHousehold` compares the normalized address on both sides, so addresses that normalize equal (e.g. `\"12 Main St\"` vs `\"12  main  street\"`) trigger the 409 household-duplicate rule.\n- `householdIdFor` derives the shared household id from the normalized address, so owners with normalized-equal addresses receive identical `householdId` values.\n\nBehavior for the other required fields, telephone/email normalization, and non-address logic is unchanged. All existing and new checkpoint tests (Cp01, Cp10, Cp11, Cp12 and the rest) pass.",
